{#
  The proposal email, plain text.

  Deterministic and template-driven, never model-written. The language model is
  allowed to write the executive summary *inside* the proposal, where every
  number it produces is validated against the snapshot before it is stored. An
  email is different: it is sent once, it cannot be corrected afterwards, and
  nobody re-reads it against the figures. So every value here is interpolated
  from the frozen snapshot and the prose around them is fixed.
#}
Hi {{ customer_name }},

Your solar proposal for {{ system_size_kwp }} kWp is ready.

You can view it here:
{{ public_url }}

At a glance
-----------
System size:        {{ system_size_kwp }} kWp ({{ panel_count }} panels)
Annual production:  {{ annual_production_kwh }} kWh
Annual saving:      EUR {{ annual_savings_eur }}
{% if payback_years -%}
Payback:            about {{ payback_years }} years
{% else -%}
Payback:            not within the 20-year analysis period
{% endif -%}
Investment:         EUR {{ capex_eur }}
{% if capacity_warning %}
Please note: {{ capacity_warning }}
{% endif %}
Reference: {{ reference }}

The figures above are estimates based on satellite imagery and modelled solar
irradiation for your roof. They are not a site survey.

{{ sender_name }}
